{"unit_id":"elysia395__dsh-wallpaper-engine#readme-32","repo":"elysia395/dsh-wallpaper-engine","commit":"3d6a272e7b547509d411760f05d37f691d02f567","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-plugin-wallpaper-engine README · Introduction：- **Wallpapers**: live Scene / Web rendering, video playback, local image / video uploads and WE project directories.\n- **Appearance**: liquid glass for settings, conversation and sidebar; colors, transparency, blur, borders and fonts.\n- **Glass subpackage**: liquid glass is a standalone subpackage row, `wallpaper-engine-glass`, which can be disabled on its own in the plugin manager; with it disabled the host — except for the wallpaper shown in the content area — returns to its native look, while wallpapers, fonts and mascots keep working.\n- **Extensions**: mascots, conversation avatars, click / pointer-trail effects, 3D parallax and optional desktop-pet integration with [dsh-pet-dshwe](https://github.com/Fish-under-sea/dsh-pet-dshwe) (a full fork of dsh-pet), installable in one click from the settings card and falling back to the native mascot when it is missing, disabled or too old.\n- **Library**: filters, hide / restore, rotation lists and whole-configuration preset import / export.","source":"extracted","section":"Introduction"}
{"unit_id":"elysia395__dsh-wallpaper-engine#readme-33","repo":"elysia395/dsh-wallpaper-engine","commit":"3d6a272e7b547509d411760f05d37f691d02f567","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-plugin-wallpaper-engine README · Introduction：| Type | How it works in DSH | Support |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Scene** | Built-in WebWallGL live rendering, with fallback chain | Supported; no WE process required |\n| **Web** | Web page mounting, WE API shim and sandboxing | Supported; depends on the page and browser |\n| **Video** | Browser playback with transcoding, fps cap and pause control | Supported |\n| **Picture** | Reads the image folder of a WE `preset` project and crossfades locally at the interval set in WE | Supported; images are never uploaded |\n| **Custom image / video** | Upload local JPG / PNG / MP4 | Supported; files stay local |","source":"extracted","section":"Introduction"}
{"unit_id":"elysia395__dsh-wallpaper-engine#readme-34","repo":"elysia395/dsh-wallpaper-engine","commit":"3d6a272e7b547509d411760f05d37f691d02f567","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-plugin-wallpaper-engine README · Introduction：Application wallpapers require launching third-party executables and are **not supported**; they never enter the library or rotation candidates.\n\n<h2 id=\"quick-start\">Quick start</h2>\n\nRequires **Node.js >= 22.12.0**, a **DSH 0.2 kernel** (including `0.2.0-rc.1/rc.2`) and **pnpm**. Close DSH completely before installing.\n\n**npm (recommended)**\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-plugin-wallpaper-engine\n```\n\nUse `desktop` instead of `web` for the desktop host.","source":"extracted","section":"Introduction"}
{"unit_id":"elysia395__dsh-wallpaper-engine#readme-35","repo":"elysia395/dsh-wallpaper-engine","commit":"3d6a272e7b547509d411760f05d37f691d02f567","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-plugin-wallpaper-engine README · Introduction：The repository ships a **multi-package release set**: installing the main package resolves the same-version subpackages (current package/tarball counts and `publishOrder` live in [RELEASING](docs/RELEASING.md); per-version changes in [CHANGELOG](docs/CHANGELOG.md)).\n\n**From source**\n\n```sh\nnode scripts/install-source.mjs --profile desktop --dsh-home \"<DSH data directory>\" --app-closed\n```","source":"extracted","section":"Introduction"}
{"unit_id":"elysia395__dsh-wallpaper-engine#readme-36","repo":"elysia395/dsh-wallpaper-engine","commit":"3d6a272e7b547509d411760f05d37f691d02f567","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-plugin-wallpaper-engine README · Introduction：Keep the source directory in place after installation. See [upgrading](docs/UPGRADING.md) and [contributing](CONTRIBUTING.md); see the [beginner guide](README.beginner.md#english) if you are new to the command line.\n\n<h2 id=\"usage\">Usage</h2>","source":"extracted","section":"Introduction"}
{"unit_id":"elysia395__dsh-wallpaper-engine#readme-37","repo":"elysia395/dsh-wallpaper-engine","commit":"3d6a272e7b547509d411760f05d37f691d02f567","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-plugin-wallpaper-engine README · Introduction：1. Open **Settings → Wallpaper Engine → Library**, or pull the mascot cord above the chat.\n2. Pick a thumbnail in the in-panel library and adjust playback / appearance; changes apply immediately and persist on the host.\n3. Pause / play controls only the current playback; clearing the current wallpaper never deletes the source file.","source":"extracted","section":"Introduction"}
{"unit_id":"elysia395__dsh-wallpaper-engine#readme-38","repo":"elysia395/dsh-wallpaper-engine","commit":"3d6a272e7b547509d411760f05d37f691d02f567","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-plugin-wallpaper-engine README · Introduction：<a href=\"https://github.com/elysia395/dsh-wallpaper-engine/releases/download/media-v1/settings-ui.gif\">\n  <img src=\"https://github.com/elysia395/dsh-wallpaper-engine/releases/download/media-v1/settings-ui.gif\" alt=\"Settings UI\">\n</a>\n\n<a href=\"https://github.com/elysia395/dsh-wallpaper-engine/releases/download/media-v1/wallpaper-library.gif\">\n  <img src=\"https://github.com/elysia395/dsh-wallpaper-engine/releases/download/media-v1/wallpaper-library.gif\" alt=\"Wallpaper library\">\n</a>","source":"extracted","section":"Introduction"}
{"unit_id":"elysia395__dsh-wallpaper-engine#readme-39","repo":"elysia395/dsh-wallpaper-engine","commit":"3d6a272e7b547509d411760f05d37f691d02f567","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-plugin-wallpaper-engine README · Introduction：- Windows, macOS and Linux share the same source. macOS has no Wallpaper Engine client: upload images / videos or point custom-wallpaper storage at WE project directories.\n- Scene rendering depends on browser WebGL and drivers; complex workshop projects may differ. Failures degrade gracefully.\n- Occlusion pause, focus-loss pause and audio loopback are platform-adapted; online lyrics are off by default.\n- When running with other skins / plugins, read [Coexistence](docs/en/HOW-IT-WORKS.md#coexistence-glass-surfaces-vs-other-ui-plugins) first.","source":"extracted","section":"Introduction"}
{"unit_id":"elysia395__dsh-wallpaper-engine#readme-40","repo":"elysia395/dsh-wallpaper-engine","commit":"3d6a272e7b547509d411760f05d37f691d02f567","type":"readme","lang":"en","text":"dsh-plugin-wallpaper-engine README · Introduction：<a href=\"https://github.com/elysia395/dsh-wallpaper-engine/releases/download/media-v1/better-sidebar-font.png\">\n  <img src=\"https://github.com/elysia395/dsh-wallpaper-engine/releases/download/media-v1/better-sidebar-font.png\" alt=\"Sidebar glass and font adaptation\">\n</a>\n\n<h2 id=\"development\">Development</h2>\n\nBug reports, platform feedback, documentation fixes and feature PRs are welcome. Include host / plugin versions, OS, wallpaper type, reproduction steps and sanitized logs.","source":"extracted","section":"Introduction"}
